\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Missing-pattern MAE across all four datasets. Three patterns: point (i.i.d.\ per cell), block (contiguous time blocks of randomly chosen sensors), and sensor (whole-sensor outages). \textsc  {Marst}\xspace  has the lowest MAE under point and block on every dataset; under sensor outage \textsc  {knn}\xspace  is competitive because it is the only method whose prediction does not depend on the absent sensor's own history.}}{20}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pattern}{{11}{20}{Missing-pattern MAE across all four datasets. Three patterns: point (i.i.d.\ per cell), block (contiguous time blocks of randomly chosen sensors), and sensor (whole-sensor outages). \MARST has the lowest MAE under point and block on every dataset; under sensor outage \KNN is competitive because it is the only method whose prediction does not depend on the absent sensor's own history}{figure.caption.23}{}}
